The frontend currently has the following:
- public/assets/{brand,fonts,icons,posters,backdrops} — 17MB
- public/media/{posters,backdrops,video} — 22MB

Next, update nginx so that /media/ first tries local files (dist/media/...) and falls back to the backend proxy:

```
location /media/ {
    try_files $uri $uri/ @media_proxy;
}
location @media_proxy {
    proxy_pass http://backend:8000;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
}
```

Wait — careful about try_files with the @ fallback: `try_files $uri $uri/ @media_proxy;` — if the file exists → serve it; otherwise → named location. ✓

Also, the /assets/ location: nginx by default serves it from the root's / (dist). The catch-all `location / { try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html; }` — for /assets/fonts/x.woff2, the file exists in dist/assets/fonts/ → try_files $uri → served. ✓

Update nginx.conf right now.

